.TH FLARE 1 "Flare" "Flare" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
flare \- serve prepared model packages on NVIDIA GPUs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B flare
.RI [ COMMAND ] " [OPTIONS]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Flare runs prepared CUDA graphs and provides an inference API.
The executable also includes a host agent and Orbit cluster management.
A compatible NVIDIA driver and a model package matching the GPU architecture
and tensor-parallel size are required for serving.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Load and serve a prepared model package.
.TP
.B agent
Run or install a host agent.
.TP
.B orbit
Pair hosts and manage multi-host serving groups.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display command help. Each subcommand also accepts this option.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display the executable version. Use dpkg-query for the Debian package version.
.SH FILES
.I /usr/share/doc/flare-inference/README.Debian
describes agent installation and upgrades.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dpkg-query (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
